msgid "Redis Cache"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default, Quarkus Cache uses Caffeine as backend.\n"
"It's possible to use Redis instead."
msgstr ""

msgid "This technology is considered {extension-status}."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In _preview_, backward compatibility and presence in the ecosystem is not "
"guaranteed.\n"
"Specific improvements might require changing configuration or APIs, and "
"plans to become _stable_ are under way.\n"
"Feedback is welcome on our https://groups.google.com/d/forum/quarkus-"
"dev[mailing list] or as issues in our https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"issues[GitHub issue tracker]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For a full list of possible statuses, check our https://quarkus.io/faq/#what-"
"are-the-extension-statuses[FAQ entry]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Redis as cache backend"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When using Redis as the backend for Quarkus cache, each cached item will be "
"stored in Redis:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The backend uses the _<default>_ Redis client (if not configured otherwise), "
"so make sure it's configured (or use the xref:redis-dev-services.adoc[Redis "
"Dev Service])"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"the Redis key is built as follows: `cache:{cache-name}:{cache-key}`, where "
"`cache-key` is the key the application uses and `cache:{cache-name}` the "
"prefix."
msgstr ""

